<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.2.2: Interpreting Statements Written in Function Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00864</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.2.2: Interpreting Statements Written in Function Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ab565fb5-dbc3-46ed-aff9-168a12d11be9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>Let’s name the functions that relate the dog’s distance from the post and the time since its owner left: function \(f\) for Day 1, function \(g\) for Day 2, function \(h\) for Day 3. The input of each function is time in seconds, \(t\).</para>
      <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-center">
        <para>Day 1<figure><media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet.  "><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_05_03_01.svg"/></media></figure></para>
        <para>Day 2<figure><media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_05_03_02.svg"/></media></figure></para>
        <para>Day 3<figure><media alt="Nonlinear function. time in seconds and distance from post in feet."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_05_03_03.svg"/></media></figure></para>
      </div>
      <para>Use <term class="glossary-tooltip">function notation</term> to complete the table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
        <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
        Day 1
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
        Day 2
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
        Day 3
      </emphasis>
            </entry>
          </row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                  <item>distance from post 60 seconds after the owner left</item>
                </list>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                  <item>distance from post when the owner left</item>
                </list>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
                  <item>distance from post 150 seconds after the owner left</item>
                </list>
              </emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
            <entry>
      </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Use function notation to represent the dog's distance from the post 60 seconds after the owner left.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution><para>a. Enter your answer for Day 1:</para><para>Compare your answer:</para>Check your response:
    Check your response:
    <para>\(f(60)\)</para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
  </problem>
        <solution><para>b. Enter your answer for Day 2:</para><para>Compare your answer:</para>Check your response:
    Check your response:
    <para>\(g(60)\)</para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
  </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>c. Enter your answer for Day 3:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(h(60)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Use function notation to represent the dog’s distance from the post when the owner left.
     </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>a. Enter your answer for Day 1:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(f(0)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
  </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>b. Enter your answer for Day 2:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(g(0)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
  </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>c. Enter your answer for Day 3:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(h(0)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Use function notation to represent the dog’s distance from the post 150 seconds after the owner left.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>a. Enter your answer for Day 1:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(f(150)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
  </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>b. Enter your answer for Day 2:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(g(150)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
  </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>c. Enter your answer for Day 3:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(h(150)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Describe what each expression represents in this context:
        <para>\(f(15)\)</para>
       </para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(f(15)\) is the distance from the post 15 seconds after the owner left on Day 1.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(g(48)\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(g(48)\) is the distance from the post 48 seconds after the owner left on Day 2.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(h(t)\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(h(t)\) is the distance from the post \(t\) seconds after the owner left on Day 3.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>The equation \(g(120)=4\) can be interpreted to mean: “On Day 2, 120 seconds after the dog owner left, the dog was 4 feet from the post.” Describe what each equation represents in this context.
        <para>\(h(40)=4.6\)</para>
       </para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>On the third day, 40 seconds after the owner left, the dog was 4.6 feet away from the post.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(f(t)=5\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>On the first day, \(t\) seconds after the owner left, the dog was 5 feet away from the post.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(g(t) = d\)</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>On the second day, \(t\) seconds after the owner left, the dog was \(d\) feet away from the post.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
